## Reviewed and confirmed clean (no changes needed)

**Database:**
- 4 tables with RLS enabled and no policy (`rate_limit_events`, `site_config`, `waitlist_status_checks`, `waitlist_status_lookups`) — deny-by-default, not exploitable.
- ~95 other anon-callable functions individually read and confirmed to already enforce `auth.uid()`/admin checks internally.
- All 13 `admin_*` functions (role grants, moderator toggling, RevHead verification, payout approval/rejection) confirmed to check `is_owner()` or `is_admin_or_moderator()` server-side, independent of the page's own UI gate.
- RLS on `dm_messages`, `group_messages`, `focus_lock_sessions`, `focus_lock_presets`, `user_wallets`, `payout_requests` all correctly scope to the resource owner or relevant group membership.

**Application code / CI:**
- `pages.yml`, `android-build.yml`, `build-desktop.yml` — credentials referenced correctly via `secrets.*`, nothing hardcoded.
- `ads.js` — reward gating is UI-only client-side; actual coin credit only happens server-side via a `service_role`-only function, so it can't be spoofed.
- `login.html` — no user-enumeration in password reset, no hardcoded secrets.
- `chat.html` — message content is properly HTML-escaped (no XSS).
- `admin.html` — admin-only access is backed by real server-side checks, not just UI hiding.
- `battle.html` — static placeholder page, no live backend logic yet.

